# Sample access list for the Mosquitto broker on the Home Assistant Yellow. NOT YET TESTED.
# It is what makes "only the governor drives actuators" and "only the user sets a plant
# type" true on the wire, not only in the code. Two broker users for the Jetson:
#   gh_core    supervisor, safety governor, store, bridge
#   gh_module  every other module

user gh_core
topic readwrite greenhouse/#
topic readwrite homeassistant/#

user gh_module
topic read greenhouse/#
topic write greenhouse/+/health
topic write greenhouse/+/config
topic write greenhouse/+/cycle
topic write greenhouse/+/output
topic write greenhouse/sensor/#
topic write greenhouse/interlock/#
topic write greenhouse/photo/#
topic write greenhouse/live/#
topic write greenhouse/capture/#
topic write greenhouse/observation/#
topic write greenhouse/vision/#
topic write greenhouse/robot/busy
topic write greenhouse/robot/bin
topic write greenhouse/gantry/state
topic write greenhouse/arm/#
topic write greenhouse/llm/#
topic write greenhouse/d405/cmd
topic write greenhouse/esphome/refresh
topic write greenhouse/safety/request
topic write greenhouse/store/cmd
topic write greenhouse/log/#
# gh_module cannot write: greenhouse/actuator/#, greenhouse/safety/request/ui,
# greenhouse/store/cmd/ui, greenhouse/+/enable, greenhouse/authority, greenhouse/kill,
# greenhouse/proposal/+/decision. Those belong to gh_core or to Home Assistant.
# Known gap: gh_module may write greenhouse/interlock/#, because the ESPHome link derives the
# interlocks. A stricter setup gives the ESPHome link its own broker user. To be decided at Gate B.
